<title>RUSSIA: Russia 3-mth T-bill yield rises to 69.12 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 3-mth T-bill yield rises to 69.12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills rose to 69.12 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 65.77 percent at the last auction on September 4, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast an average yield in the 75- to 85-percent range.  </p>
<p>Full details of the auction:</p>
<p>				    Sept 25	    Sept 4</p>
<p>    Series number	     21071		21070</p>
<p>    Issue volume		4.00 trln rbls  3.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	    7.90 trln	 5.24 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    3.91 trln	 3.05 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    3.19 trln	 2.50 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    81.61 pct	  82.10 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	    69.12 pct	  65.77 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  81.51 pct	  81.80 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield 69.58 pct	  67.12 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 119 days	  121 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		  Sept 25	   Sept 4</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     Jan 22, 1997    Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p>On September 25, the finance ministry will also auction seven trillion roubles in six-month T-bills. It will also repay about seven trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
